Subject: [PATCH v13 2/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Let Dovecot write the list
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: nsosnlpzqvrykposnmmpnxsymltpzpsy
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:55:03 +0000

While mbsync writes the maildir and Dovecot only reads it, as another
user, nothing else can change the list: a post or an archive would
need a third writer, and every new message waits for a job to open up
its file before Dovecot can serve it. With Dovecot as the only writer
and mbsync as one of its IMAP clients, any later writer goes through
Dovecot too.

- vmail owns the maildir. mbsync fetches into Dovecot over IMAP, as
  the login mbsync, so the fetch job no longer opens up its files.
- Dovecot checks the logins in imap-users against their passwords.
  Every other user name still logs in with any password, and the ACL,
  now taken only from the global file, lets it only read.
- The spec gains a rights section, and says that a reader's STORE or
  EXPUNGE answers OK and changes nothing, as Dovecot does.
- check covers the new secrets and the maildir's new owner.
- README.org has the operator empty the maildir and mbsync's state
  before the first fetch into Dovecot.
